course: dictionary
lesson: 8755
title: Settler
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A settler is a person who moves to a new place to live there for good and make a home. «Many of Australia's first settlers came from London, south-east England and Ireland.» The clue is "came from" and "first": they arrived in a new land and stayed.
explain: In history, settlers came from another country and took land to farm and build towns. «Europeans brought diseases like smallpox that killed very many people, and later settlers pushed Native nations off their lands.» Here the clues show that the land was already someone's home, so the word can carry a sad side too.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Homesick settlers named the American robin» can become «Homesick people who moved to a new land named the American robin», and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Settler also has a rare meaning: something that settles a matter, like a final point that ends an argument. In history and geography lessons, you will almost always meet the first meaning, about people.
fact: A settler is a person who moves to a new place to live there for good.
fact: In history, settlers were people who came from another country and took land to farm and build towns.
fact: Phrases you may meet are early settlers, the first settlers, European settlers and settler families.
fact: Often the land was already home to other peoples, such as the First Nations, Aboriginal and Māori peoples, whose land was taken.
fact: The rare meaning of settler is something that settles a matter, like a final point that ends an argument.
exercise: «Many of Australia's first settlers came from London and Ireland.» What is a settler? | A visitor who stays only one night | A person who sits down to rest after a long walk | *A person who moves to a new place to live there for good | A shopkeeper who sells food
exercise: «Later settlers pushed Native nations off their lands.» What does this tell us? | Settlers never met Native nations | Settlers gave Native nations new land for free | *Settlers took land that other peoples already lived on | Native nations moved to London
exercise: «Homesick settlers named the American robin because its red breast reminded them of home.» Why did they choose that name? | It had no name at all in England | It was the first bird they saw in America | *Its red breast reminded them of home | It could sing like a bell
test: In the sentence «The first settlers built log cabins and farmed the land», what are the settlers doing? | *Moving to a new land to live and make a home | Visiting for one afternoon only | Digging for gold and then leaving | Selling their cabins to visitors
test: Which is the rare meaning of settler? | A sleepy bird | A hut made of logs | *Something that ends an argument for good | A person who moves to a new land to live
exam: Why can the story of settlers be a sad one? | Settlers never farmed the land | Settlers only ever built schools | *Settlers often pushed other peoples off land that was already their home | Settlers always arrived in empty lands
